<p class="mt-align-center"><img alt="2.jpg" style="max-width: 748px;" class="internal" loading="lazy" src="https://chem.libretexts.org/@api/deki/files/13451/2.jpg?revision=1" /></p>

<p class="mt-align-center"><img src="data:image/png;base64," style="width: 657px; height: 88px;" /></p>
</div></section>

<p>In biological systems, ester formation occurs through a similar process except thioester or acyl adenosyl phosphates are used instead of carboxylic acid chlorides. These reaction will be discussed in more detail in <strong>Chapter 21</strong>.</p>

<p class="mt-align-center"><img src="data:image/png;base64," /></p>

